@unattended-budget-guards
Feature: Unattended build-profile budget guards
  As the operator of the unattended build service
  I want every build to run under a named budget profile with hard caps
  So that an overnight build can never churn or overrun unnoticed — it pauses and asks me

  Background:
    Given the configuration defines an "attended" profile with no caps
    And it defines an "unattended" profile with conservative caps

  # Why: attended = reviewer-driven, no numeric cap (ASSUM-010 preserved)
  # [SKELETON-SATISFIED] tests/forge/pipeline/test_budget_guard.py::TestAttendedNeverBreaches
  @key-example @smoke @task:TASK-UBS-002-skeleton
  Scenario: An attended build is never constrained by budget caps
    Given a build running under the attended profile
    When the budget guard evaluates the build after many review cycles and long runtime
    Then the build is judged within budget

  # Why: core happy path — an unattended build below every cap runs freely
  # [SKELETON-SATISFIED] test_budget_guard.py::TestCapBreaches::test_review_cycle_below_cap_ok
  @key-example @smoke @task:TASK-UBS-002-skeleton
  Scenario: An unattended build below all its caps is judged within budget
    Given a build running under the unattended profile
    And the build is below every configured cap
    When the budget guard evaluates the build
    Then the build is judged within budget

